  "description": "T002 - Tag 1658 - Robinia Re-pollard. Growing within a restricted planting area, with root development contributing to displacement of the low retaining wall. Areas of delaminated bark present up to 2mH. No fungal fruiting bodies observed. Approximately 3-4m of regrowth since the most recent pruning cycle, maintain the existing pruning regime. T004 - Tag 1660 - Robinia Re-pollard. Growing within a raised planter, creating a restricted rooting environment. Asymmetrical stem with a southerly lean, bifurcating at 3mH. Root development is contributing to displacement of the low retaining wall. Approximately 3-4m of regrowth since the most recent pruning cycle, maintain the existing pruning regime. ",
